  "name": "Example: Expressions With Integer Bases",
  "problem": "Express $\\dfrac{(-5)^{7}}{(-5)^3}$ as a base raised to a single exponent.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write the fraction as a division:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(-5)^{7}}{(-5)^3} = (-5)^{7} \\div (-5)^3\n$$\n\nNow, to divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n(-5)^{7} \\div (-5)^3 = (-5)^{7-3} = (-5)^{4}\n$$",
